## Named for the lane that owns it (not this row's cell)

- The built-in code layout's interior (codeDefaultLayoutInterior in
  page.ts) splices {{_main}} through an ordinary programmatic nest, which
  for an unknown main card takes the nested :unknown posture (empty for a
  viewer who may not create) where Ruby's chunk dispatch splices
  main.rendered (the not_found frame). On a card-layout deck (every real
  deck; the recorded harness pages) the splice goes through mainNest and
  the frame lands; the entry-point suite seeds the card-layout lane for
  its full-page pins for exactly that reason. Changing the code lane's
  interior would move every known-card code-layout page's slot bytes, so
  it is named here for the layout lane, not changed in this row.
- The bare render entry (RenderEngine#render, the hosts' renderSlot
  seam) still refuses an unknown name; the nested :unknown posture, not
  the main+root arm, is its surface. Pinned in both the parity test and
  the entry-point suite.

